# Start-from set for the Aeneas lift of `crates/lattice` (charon `--start-from`).
# One item path per line; blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.
#
# After editing this file, regenerate the committed Lean model with
#   nix run .#extract          (or: scripts/extract.sh inside `nix develop .#extraction`)
# and commit the result. CI's `extraction-drift` workflow regenerates and
# `git diff`s the model, so a stale model fails the build.
#
# NOTE: charon's `--start-from` for inherent impl methods is finicky
# (`crate::small::SmallRat::reduce` silently matches nothing). We instead lift the
# whole `small` module — which pulls in `SmallRat::reduce` and its dependency
# closure — and name `sign_variations` directly. See
# docs/spike-extraction-report.md and docs/upgrading-extraction-toolchain.md.

crate::sturm::sign_variations
crate::small

# The reference bignum (algebra-rehaul R.4b): `RefBackend`, an independent
# `Vec<u64>`-limb sign-magnitude `Backend` (schoolbook add/sub/mul, bit-serial
# long-division divrem, Euclid gcd). Lifted so each op can be PROVEN = Mathlib
# ℤ/ℚ over a limb→ℕ denotation (docs/refbackend-lift.md), turning the dashu
# differential into a proof-backed oracle. Unlike the certify-core lift, `rat`/
# `backend` are NOT opaque here — the whole point is to lift the concrete limb
# arithmetic. Pulls in the `Backend` trait def (dup-free since R.3a) + RefNat/
# RefInt/RefRat + normalize.
crate::refbackend
